<title>NEW ZEALAND: Milburn gloomy on China cement co prospects.</title>
<headline>Milburn gloomy on China cement co prospects.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of building materials group Milburn New Zealand Limited said on Friday he felt a rapid turn-around was unlikely in the performance of the Golden Cat cement company in Suzhau, China.</p>
<p>Milburn has a 25 percent interest in the joint venture.</p>
<p>Bob Stannard told Milburn's annual meeting that expected production and distribution efficiencies in China &quot;would put Milburn in a position to benefit from a relaxation of economic constraints and market improvement&quot;.</p>
<p>--Wellington newsroom +64 4 471 4273</p>
</text>
